StackPulse is a native, from-scratch implementation. It is not a fork. It does,
however, stand on the shoulders of prior open-source work. This NOTICE records
what we studied, what we incorporated, and what we merely referenced, so that
attribution is accurate and honest.

================================================================================
1. OpenUsage — incorporated as an attributed reference (parsing/pricing logic)
================================================================================

Project:        OpenUsage
Repository:     https://github.com/robinebers/openusage
Upstream ref:   v0.7.5
License:        MIT
Copyright:      (c) 2026 Robin Ebers

What we did:
  OpenUsage is a macOS menu-bar usage monitor written almost entirely in Swift.
  StackPulse's non-negotiable design requirement is a PORTABLE Rust core that
  can be reused by non-macOS clients (a future Windows app and a Chrome
  native-messaging host). A predominantly-Swift application cannot provide that
  core, so StackPulse is NOT a hard fork of OpenUsage.

  Instead, we studied OpenUsage's provider log-parsing and cost-estimation
  approach and RE-IMPLEMENTED the equivalent logic in Rust
  (crates/stackpulse-core), and we reimplemented the macOS application natively
  in Swift (apps/StackPulseMac). Concepts adapted from OpenUsage include the
  overall idea of scanning provider session logs locally, the shape of the
  Claude Code and Codex CLI on-disk formats, and cost estimation from an
  embedded price table.

  No OpenUsage source CODE is copied verbatim into this repository. All Rust and
  Swift in this repository was written for StackPulse. Where our behavior
  intentionally matches OpenUsage's (for example, path resolution order,
  token-deduplication semantics, or which vendor endpoint answers a given
  question), that is by design and is credited here.

  ONE ASSET IS COPIED. The provider brand marks in
  apps/StackPulseMac/Sources/StackPulseApp/ProviderMarks.swift are the SVG path
  data from OpenUsage's Sources/OpenUsage/Resources/ProviderIcons/*.svg,
  re-keyed to StackPulse's provider ids and embedded as Swift string literals.
  That artwork is redistributed here under OpenUsage's MIT license (reproduced
  below). The menu-bar strip layout (a brand mark beside one large reading, or
  two stacked tight lines) also follows OpenUsage's design.

Trademarks:
  OpenUsage ships a TRADEMARK.md. The "OpenUsage" name and marks are NOT reused
  by StackPulse. "StackPulse" is an independent name. Do not present StackPulse
  as OpenUsage, a fork of OpenUsage, or as endorsed by the OpenUsage project.

  AI PROVIDER MARKS. StackPulse embeds the brand marks of the AI tools it
  monitors (Anthropic/Claude, OpenAI/Codex, GitHub Copilot, Cursor,
  Antigravity, Devin, Grok/xAI, OpenCode, OpenRouter, Z.ai) so a menu-bar
  reading can say which tool it belongs to. Each mark remains the trademark of
  its owner and is used here for IDENTIFICATION ONLY — nominative use. Their
  presence does not imply any affiliation with, sponsorship by, or endorsement
  from those vendors. StackPulse is an independent, unaffiliated tool.

The OpenUsage MIT license text is reproduced in full at the end of this file.

================================================================================
2. CodexBar — referenced for ideas (not incorporated)
================================================================================

Project:        CodexBar
Repository:     https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar
License:        MIT

What we did:
  We reviewed CodexBar for ideas on surfacing OpenAI Codex CLI rate-limit
  windows and session state in a macOS menu bar. No CodexBar source code is
  included in this repository. Our Codex adapter (crates/stackpulse-core,
  providers/codex.rs) was written independently from the documented Codex CLI
  session-log format.

================================================================================
3. Tokcat — referenced for ideas (not incorporated)
================================================================================

Project:        Tokcat
Repository:     https://github.com/handlecusion/tokcat
Stack:          Tauri (Rust + web front end)

What we did:
  We reviewed Tokcat, a Tauri-based token/usage viewer, for interaction and
  presentation ideas. No Tokcat source code is included in this repository.

